# catalog/lane-run-inputs.d/pipeline-health.rw — the per-project files one
# `bin/pipeline-health.sh --project $p` run writes. A write-back may carry
# these only. The ro snapshot is these plus pipeline-health.ro. The inventory,
# with file:line for each entry, is in
# docs/notes/2026-10-14-BH-6719-lane-run-inputs-manifests.md.
#
# The fleet-wide files a project run also writes, one choice per file
# (BH-6892, docs/notes/2026-10-16-BH-6892-pipeline-health-offhub.md):
#   state/health-active.txt      @rows below: this project's PH_PROJ_NS keys
#                                (PH_PROJ_NS in bin/pipeline-health.sh, the
#                                epilogue's owned()); the epilogue lock is the apply lock
#   state/health-active.stamp    not written on a machine (`# >>> active stamp`)
#   state/health-alerted.json    read-only on a machine: the run keeps its
#                                stamps in state/pipeline-health/$p/alerted.json
#                                (`# >>> machine dedup`)
#   state/closeout-aged-out.tsv  @rows below; every writer takes <path>.lock
#                                (checks 4 and 5, bin/disk-clean.sh step 4)
#   logs/ALERTS.log              not written: every line is a POST to
#                                /api/alert-lines (alert_emit, the epilogue)
#   state/alert-line-sent/*, state/alerts/*,
#   logs/alerts-state.log        not written: no beat.sh call on a machine;
#                                the hub's replay of each line writes them
#   state/alert-quarantine.jsonl not written anywhere for a machine alert: the
#                                replay beats kind:"alert", and beat.sh
#                                quarantines only kind:"fleet_alert"
#   /root/repos/$p refs          not read: stale-parent reads GitHub REST
#                                (`# >>> stale parent`, bin/lib/stale-parent-rest.sh)
# Secrets, locks and machine-local caches are never carried: env/*, locks/*,
# state/gh-*, state/gh-budget/*, state/settings-cache.json, state/lane-gate/*,
# state/pr-snapshot/*.
# logs/pipeline-health.log rides back as the lane log (.lri/log-append).
#
# closeout-aged.tsv: bin/lib/closeout-terminal.sh:173-252
state/pipeline-health/$p/*
# bin/pipeline-health.sh:998-1004
state/pipeline-health/noprogress/$p.stranded
state/pipeline-health/noprogress/$p.parked
# bin/pipeline-health.sh:421-422
flags/pool-halt-$p
# bin/pipeline-health.sh epilogue (the retraction pass). The ERE's list is
# PH_PROJ_NS of bin/pipeline-health.sh; tests/pipeline-health-offhub.bh-6892-test.sh M1 pins it.
state/health-active.txt
@rows state/health-active.txt ^(stuckqueue|poolhalt|uncommented|emptyurl|staleremote|tickloop|stalepr|starved|strandedqueue|staledequeue|staleparent|noprogress|stalehold|stalledblocker):$p(:|$)
# bin/lib/closeout-terminal.sh:148 (rows are proj TAB builddir TAB ...)
state/closeout-aged-out.tsv
@rows state/closeout-aged-out.tsv ^$p[[:space:]]
